Crystal Hill is a luxury apartment building in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Diamond District/index|Diamond District]], its lobby a fane whose interior looks like the inside of a cut gemstone. The walls branch up and close into a dome, and the floor reads as a single polished sheet of diamond. Outside, the sidewalk glitters with what look like gemstones set into the asphalt, a shine that grows stronger as one nears the front doors. There is no doorman at the entrance, just two open doors, and no place to linger: the uncomfortable lounge chairs near the front are not for waiting. You are here either to visit a resident or to leave one.

Four banks of paternosters stand opposite the entrance, platforms of softly rumbling crystal that rise and fall in a continuous loop, and riders step on and off as they pass. The building keeps a pair of armed staff behind a desk grown from the floor in harder purple crystal, both in deep red suits with little red bellhop hats. One of them is a taller lizardfolk man with light red scales.
